---
Part XIV: The landing
Chapter 1: The landing styles
Package: design/src/
Language: CSS
---

# The landing styles

The landing dresses itself as a code editor. Its palette is a deep editor slate with a handful of syntax accents, its type pairs a serif display face with a monospace body, and a faint vertical grid runs behind everything like a gutter. This chapter is that stylesheet — the tokens, the base, and the look of each region the later chapters build. Every value is a token, so the whole page turns on the variables at the top.

## The tokens and the base

The tokens name the palette and the faces. The backgrounds layer the page from the darkest surface up. The foregrounds ramp from bright text to the faintest label. The accents are the syntax colours — a cyan, a mint, a violet, an amber, a rose — and the mint is the primary, the colour a selection and a live mark wear. A shadow token holds the drop a raised panel casts.

The page carries a second palette for the light theme. A `data-theme` attribute set to light on the root swaps every colour token to its light value — a warm Gruvbox cream ground, ink foregrounds, and accents in a rust-and-olive duo — while the faces stay the same. Because every rule reads a token, the whole page turns on that one attribute.

The light theme leads with a rust duo — a warm terracotta set led by an olive-green primary — the default the base rule sets. Seven more families sit behind a `data-accent` attribute the tweaks panel switches. Four are earthy, one warm-to-green arc at a muted tone: a terracotta rust, a golden ochre, a khaki olive, and a green moss. Three break that calm on purpose: a hot fuchsia, an electric blue, and a vivid grape. Each family overrides only the six accent tokens, so the ground and the text hold still while the accents change.

The base sets the page in the mono face on the slate. Every face ends in Noto Color Emoji, so an emoji the page shows — the game's bomb, its blast — renders the same on every client rather than in each platform's own set.

=>

:root {
  --bg:        #0F1014;
  --bg-2:      #15171D;
  --bg-3:      #1B1E26;
  --bg-4:      #232732;
  --rule:      #FFFFFF12;
  --rule-2:    #FFFFFF1F;
  --fg:        #E6E6EA;
  --fg-2:      #B6B8C2;
  --fg-3:      #7A7E8C;
  --fg-4:      #4D5260;

  --acc-cyan:   #6CC7E0;
  --acc-mint:   #8FE0B6;
  --acc-violet: #B59BF1;
  --acc-amber:  #E8B86C;
  --acc-rose:   #E48A9A;
  --acc-grey:   #8A92A6;

  --primary:   var(--acc-mint);
  --shadow:    #000000B0;

  --display: 'Newsreader', Georgia, 'Noto Color Emoji', serif;
  --sans:    'iA Writer Quattro', 'iA Writer Quattro S', system-ui, -apple-system, 'Noto Color Emoji', sans-serif;
  --mono:    'JetBrains Mono', ui-monospace, Menlo, 'Noto Color Emoji', monospace;
}

:root[data-theme="light"] {
  --bg:        #F2E5BC;
  --bg-2:      #EBDBB2;
  --bg-3:      #D5C4A1;
  --bg-4:      #BDAE93;
  --rule:      #3C38361A;
  --rule-2:    #3C383633;
  --fg:        #3C3836;
  --fg-2:      #504945;
  --fg-3:      #665C54;
  --fg-4:      #928374;

  --acc-cyan:   #913C30;
  --acc-mint:   #699130;
  --acc-violet: #918430;
  --acc-amber:  #913044;
  --acc-rose:   #769130;
  --acc-grey:   #7B6D65;

  --shadow:    #79695033;
}

:root[data-theme="light"][data-accent="rust"] {
  --acc-cyan:   #913C30;
  --acc-mint:   #915430;
  --acc-violet: #918430;
  --acc-amber:  #913044;
  --acc-rose:   #769130;
  --acc-grey:   #7B6D65;
}
:root[data-theme="light"][data-accent="ochre"] {
  --acc-cyan:   #916630;
  --acc-mint:   #917E30;
  --acc-violet: #749130;
  --acc-amber:  #914730;
  --acc-rose:   #4C9130;
  --acc-grey:   #7B7765;
}
:root[data-theme="light"][data-accent="olive"] {
  --acc-cyan:   #917C30;
  --acc-mint:   #8E9130;
  --acc-violet: #5E9130;
  --acc-amber:  #915E30;
  --acc-rose:   #359130;
  --acc-grey:   #7B7B65;
}
:root[data-theme="light"][data-accent="moss"] {
  --acc-cyan:   #309139;
  --acc-mint:   #309151;
  --acc-violet: #309181;
  --acc-amber:  #479130;
  --acc-rose:   #307991;
  --acc-grey:   #657B6C;
}
:root[data-theme="light"][data-accent="fuchsia"] {
  --acc-cyan:   #AD1F8E;
  --acc-mint:   #AD1F6B;
  --acc-violet: #AD1F23;
  --acc-amber:  #9F1FAD;
  --acc-rose:   #AD551F;
  --acc-grey:   #825E71;
}
:root[data-theme="light"][data-accent="electric"] {
  --acc-cyan:   #1F96AD;
  --acc-mint:   #1F72AD;
  --acc-violet: #1F2AAD;
  --acc-amber:  #1FAD98;
  --acc-rose:   #4E1FAD;
  --acc-grey:   #5E7382;
}
:root[data-theme="light"][data-accent="grape"] {
  --acc-cyan:   #471FAD;
  --acc-mint:   #6B1FAD;
  --acc-violet: #AD1FA9;
  --acc-amber:  #1F23AD;
  --acc-rose:   #AD1F6D;
  --acc-grey:   #715E82;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html, body { margin: 0; padding: 0; }
body {
  background: var(--bg);
  color: var(--fg);
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 14px;
  line-height: 1.55;
  -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
::selection { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--primary) 35%, transparent); color: var(--fg); }

main, header, footer { position: relative; }

.wrap { max-width: 1280px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 32px; }

## The window chrome

The page wears a window's chrome. A title bar runs across the top: the Loom logo on the left — its woven mark beside the wordmark — and the theme switch on the right. Below it a tab bar carries the site's menu as a row of open tabs, drawn on the page's own colour so the tabs read as tabs, with a link to the source at its right end. Both bars stay sticky, so the chrome holds while the content scrolls.

=>

.titlebar {
  height: 44px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  background: var(--bg-2);
  display: flex; align-items: center;
  padding: 0 16px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 60;
}
.title-logo { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; color: var(--fg); }
.title-mark { display: inline-flex; color: var(--acc-mint); }
.title-mark svg { width: 22px; height: 22px; }
.title-word {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 16px; font-weight: 600;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  color: var(--fg);
}
.titlebar .right {
  margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: 14px; align-items: center;
  color: var(--fg-3);
}
.titlebar .right kbd,
.tabbar .right kbd {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  padding: 1px 6px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  background: var(--bg-3);
}
.theme-switch {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  width: 26px; height: 26px;
  padding: 0;
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 6px;
  background: var(--bg-3);
  color: var(--fg-3);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: color .15s ease, border-color .15s ease, background .15s ease;
}
.theme-switch:hover { color: var(--fg); border-color: var(--fg-4); background: var(--bg-4); }
.theme-switch svg { display: block; }

.tabbar {
  display: flex; align-items: stretch;
  background: var(--bg);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  height: 40px;
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px;
  position: sticky; top: 44px; z-index: 55;
}
.tab {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;
  padding: 0 16px;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  text-decoration: none;
  cursor: pointer;
  position: relative;
  box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 0 transparent;
  transition: color .15s ease, background .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease;
}
.tab.active {
  color: var(--fg);
  box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 0 0 var(--primary);
}
.tab:hover:not(.active) { color: var(--fg-2); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 6%, transparent); }
.tab .dot {
  width: 6px; height: 6px; border-radius: 50%;
  background: var(--acc-cyan);
}
.tab:nth-child(2) .dot { background: var(--acc-violet); }
.tab:nth-child(3) .dot { background: var(--acc-amber); }
.tab:nth-child(4) .dot { background: var(--acc-mint); }
.tabbar .right {
  margin-left: auto; display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center;
  padding: 0 14px;
  color: var(--fg-3);
}
.tabbar .right .bar-github {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
  transition: color .15s ease;
}
.tabbar .right .bar-github:hover { color: var(--fg); }

## The hero and its rotating headline

The hero is the first screen: the Loom logo set large, then two columns. On the left is the pitch — the headline and the install rows beneath it; on the right, a short statement of what Loom is, a lead line and four points each marked with the loom mark, the calls to action beneath. The two columns align at the top, so the statement starts level with the headline. The headline is set large in the display serif, and one word of it rotates — swapping on a blur-and-slide transition — with a blinking caret after it. Its three lines carry three colours: plain text, then mint, then violet on the rotating line. A `data-title` of two folds that to two colours, the rotating line taking the mint. Below a set width the two columns fall into one, the statement below the pitch.

=>

.hero {
  padding: 96px 0 64px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.hero-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1fr);
  gap: 56px;
  align-items: start;
}
@media (max-width: 1080px) {
  .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 44px; }
}
.hero-col {
  max-width: 680px;
}

.gutter-row {
  display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 18px;
  color: var(--fg-4);
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px;
  margin-bottom: 6px;
}
.gutter { color: var(--fg-4); width: 22px; text-align: right; user-select: none; flex-shrink: 0; }

.hero-logo {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 40px;
}
.hero-logo-mark { display: inline-flex; color: var(--acc-mint); }
.hero-logo-mark svg { width: 46px; height: 46px; }
.hero-logo-word {
  font-family: var(--display);
  font-weight: 300;
  font-size: 46px;
  line-height: 1;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  color: var(--fg);
}
.hero-logo-ver {
  align-self: center;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 12px;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 999px;
  padding: 3px 9px;
}

h1.loom-h {
  font-family: var(--display);
  font-weight: 300;
  font-size: clamp(36px, 4.6vw, 65px);
  line-height: 1.2;
  letter-spacing: -0.025em;
  margin: 0;
  color: var(--fg);
  text-wrap: balance;
}
h1.loom-h .hl-1 { color: var(--fg); }
h1.loom-h .hl-2 { color: var(--acc-mint); }
h1.loom-h .hl-3 { color: var(--acc-violet); }
:root[data-title="two"] h1.loom-h .hl-3 { color: var(--acc-mint); }
.rotator-host {
  display: inline-block;
  position: relative;
}
.rotator-word {
  display: inline-block;
  transition: opacity .35s ease, transform .35s ease, filter .35s ease;
}
.rotator-word.out { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(-0.18em); filter: blur(3px); }
.rotator-word.in-start { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(0.18em); filter: blur(3px); }
.caret {
  display: inline-block;
  width: 0.5ch; height: 1em;
  background: var(--acc-mint);
  margin-left: 0.2em;
  vertical-align: -0.2em;
  animation: blink 1.05s steps(2) infinite;
}
@keyframes blink { 0%,50% { opacity: 1; } 50.01%,100% { opacity: 0; } }

.hero-note {
  max-width: 30em;
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 17px;
  line-height: 1.7;
  color: var(--fg-2);
}
.hero-note p { margin: 0 0 18px; }
.hero-note p:last-child { margin: 0; }
.hero-note .hero-lead { color: var(--fg); }
.hero-points {
  list-style: none;
  margin: 20px 0;
  padding: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 14px;
}
.hero-points li { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; }
.hero-bullet { flex-shrink: 0; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; height: 1.7em; color: var(--acc-amber); }
.hero-prim {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 0.86em;
  color: var(--acc-cyan);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-cyan) 12%, transparent);
  padding: 1px 5px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

## The call to action

Below the install rows sit the calls to action, a row of two buttons — read the docs, browse the source. Each is a quiet slate pill, the primary one in mint. A hard shadow in a darker shade of the button's own colour lifts it off the page to the lower right, the way an old desktop button stood proud of its surface. Hovering presses the button toward that shadow, and the shadow shrinks to meet it.

=>

.actions {
  margin-top: 40px;
  display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center;
}
.btn {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  padding: 11px 16px;
  background: var(--bg-3);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  color: var(--fg);
  border-radius: 6px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 13px;
  cursor: pointer;
  --btn-shadow: color-mix(in srgb, var(--bg-3) 72%, #000);
  box-shadow: 2px 2px 0 0 var(--btn-shadow);
  transition: background .15s ease, border-color .15s ease, transform .15s ease, box-shadow .15s ease;
}
.btn:hover { background: var(--bg-4); border-color: var(--fg-4); transform: translate(1px, 1px); box-shadow: 1px 1px 0 0 var(--btn-shadow); }
.btn:active { transform: translate(2px, 2px); box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 var(--btn-shadow); }
.btn.primary {
  background: var(--acc-mint);
  color: var(--bg);
  border-color: var(--acc-mint);
  font-weight: 500;
  --btn-shadow: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-mint) 72%, #000);
}
.btn.primary:hover { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-mint) 90%, white); }
.keys {
  color: var(--fg-3);
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12px;
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px;
  margin-left: 6px;
}
.keys kbd {
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  background: var(--bg-3);
  color: var(--fg-2);
  border-radius: 4px;
  padding: 2px 6px;
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px;
}

## The shared panel head

Every panel on the page — the workspace config, the file tree, the step detail — frames itself the same way: a small head naming what it holds, a dot, and a right-aligned label. `panel-head` is that one shared chrome, so a reader learns to read a panel once.

=>

.panel-head {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  height: 30px; padding: 0 12px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  background: var(--bg-3);
  color: var(--fg-3);
  font-size: 11px;
}
.panel-head .dot { width: 7px; height: 7px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--acc-mint); }
.panel-head .right {
  margin-left: auto; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;
  color: var(--fg-4);
}

## The numbered sections

The body divides into numbered sections, each with a small eyebrow number and a display heading.

=>

section.s {
  padding: 88px 0;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.sec-head {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  gap: 14px;
  margin-bottom: 32px;
}
.sec-num {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 14px;
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  text-transform: uppercase;
}
.sec-num .arrow { color: var(--acc-mint); margin-right: 6px; }
.sec-h {
  font-family: var(--display);
  font-weight: 300;
  font-size: clamp(30px, 4vw, 48px);
  line-height: 1.1;
  letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  margin: 0 0 18px;
  color: var(--fg);
  max-width: 22ch;
  text-wrap: balance;
}
.sec-lede {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  color: var(--fg-2);
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.6;
  max-width: 60ch;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}

## How it works — the tabbed panel

The how-it-works section gives its width to one panel, an editor with three tabs: the loom, the tangled TypeScript, and the playable game. The loom tab reads as its raw source or, at the flick of a switch, as a rendered document. Every document view sets its canvas beside an outline that stays in view as the page scrolls: the preview lists the example's headings, the raw source the loom's own, the tangle the symbols it exports behind a muted chip for each one's kind. A row in any of them jumps to its target and lifts to mint. The tangle tab holds the whole file, coloured at build time in both of the landing's palettes so the code turns light or dark with the page. The panel grows to the height of whatever it shows, so the page carries the scroll and nothing nests inside; only the game keeps a fixed height, a square board that stays in reach. The board tells the two sides apart by colour. The reader plays the violet stones and the engine the mint, and the light theme returns both to plain black and white. Prose reads as prose, code keeps its syntax colour, and an anchor the loom has not resolved stays violet. The prose holds a measure of a hundred characters, so a line stays readable instead of running the full width of the pane.

=>

.how-detail {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  position: relative;
}

.ex-tabs {
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  flex-shrink: 0;
  gap: 6px;
  height: 38px;
  position: relative;
  z-index: 1;
}
.ex-tab {
  appearance: none;
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 7px;
  background: var(--bg-3);
  color: var(--fg-3);
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 12px;
  height: 30px;
  margin-bottom: 4px;
  padding: 0 16px;
  cursor: pointer;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  transition: background .12s ease, color .12s ease, height .12s ease;
}
.ex-tab.play { margin-left: auto; }
.ex-tab:hover:not(.active) { color: var(--fg-2); background: var(--bg-4); }
.ex-tab.active {
  color: var(--fg);
  background: var(--bg-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-bottom: none;
  border-radius: 7px 7px 0 0;
  height: 38px;
  margin-bottom: -1px;
}

.how-body {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  background: var(--bg-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 0 0 8px 8px;
}
.how-body.capped {
  max-height: clamp(572px, 94vh, 936px);
  overflow: hidden;
  position: relative;
}
.how-expand {
  position: absolute;
  inset: auto 0 0 0;
  height: 200px;
  display: flex;
  align-items: flex-end;
  justify-content: center;
  padding: 0 0 30px;
  border: 0;
  background: transparent;
  cursor: pointer;
}
.how-expand::before {
  content: '';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, var(--bg-2) 85%);
  -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(2.5px);
  backdrop-filter: blur(2.5px);
  -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, #000 45%);
  mask-image: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, #000 45%);
}
.how-expand-label {
  position: relative;
  display: inline-flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 8px;
  padding: 9px 18px;
  border-radius: 999px;
  background: var(--acc-violet);
  color: var(--bg);
  font-family: var(--sans);
  font-size: 13px;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.01em;
  transition: background .16s ease;
}
.how-expand:hover .how-expand-label {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-violet) 70%, #fff);
  animation: expandNudge 0.5s ease-out;
}
@keyframes expandNudge {
  0% { transform: translateY(0); }
  45% { transform: translateY(-6px); }
  100% { transform: translateY(0); }
}
.ex-icon { display: inline-flex; }
.ex-icon.white { color: var(--fg); }
.ex-icon.green { color: var(--acc-mint); }
.tab-badge {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 9px;
  font-weight: 600;
  line-height: 1;
  padding: 2px 4px;
  border-radius: 3px;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
}
.tab-badge.white {
  color: var(--fg);
  border-color: var(--rule-2);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--fg) 8%, transparent);
}

.how-loom {
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
}
.loom-toggle {
  display: flex;
  gap: 4px;
  padding: 28px 56px 0;
}
.loom-toggle-btn {
  appearance: none;
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 6px;
  background: transparent;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  letter-spacing: 0.04em;
  padding: 5px 12px;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background .12s ease, color .12s ease;
}
.loom-toggle-btn:hover { color: var(--fg-2); background: var(--bg-3); }
.loom-toggle-btn.active { color: var(--fg); background: var(--bg-3); }

.how-scroll {
  padding: 56px;
}

.how-preview {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 208px;
  align-items: start;
}
@media (max-width: 880px) {
  .how-preview { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  .how-outline { display: none; }
}
.how-outline {
  position: sticky;
  top: 96px;
  align-self: start;
  max-height: calc(100vh - 116px);
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 40px 16px 24px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 12px;
}
.how-outline-row {
  padding: 5px 8px;
  border-radius: 4px;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background .12s ease, color .12s ease;
}
.how-outline-row:hover { color: var(--fg); background: var(--bg-3); }
.how-outline-row.active {
  color: var(--acc-mint);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-mint) 12%, transparent);
}
.how-outline-kind {
  margin-right: 7px;
  color: var(--fg-4);
  font-size: 10px;
}

.how-file-title {
  font-family: var(--display);
  font-weight: 300;
  font-size: 30px;
  line-height: 1.15;
  letter-spacing: -0.015em;
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  color: var(--fg);
}
.how-section-h {
  font-family: var(--display);
  font-weight: 300;
  font-size: 22px;
  line-height: 1.2;
  letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  margin: 36px 0 12px;
  scroll-margin-top: 96px;
  color: var(--fg);
  transition: color .15s ease;
}
.how-section-h.active { color: var(--acc-mint); }
.how-spec {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 0.6em;
  font-weight: 500;
  letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  color: var(--acc-cyan);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-cyan) 12%, transparent);
  padding: 2px 8px;
  border-radius: 6px;
  vertical-align: middle;
  margin-left: 0.5em;
}

.how-prose { margin: 0; max-width: 100ch; }
.how-prose p {
  font-family: var(--sans);
  color: var(--fg-2);
  font-size: 16px;
  line-height: 1.72;
  margin: 0 0 16px;
  text-wrap: pretty;
}
.how-prose code {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 0.9em;
  color: var(--acc-cyan);
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-cyan) 12%, transparent);
  padding: 1px 5px;
  border-radius: 4px;
}

.shiki,
.shiki span {
  color: var(--shiki-dark);
  font-style: var(--shiki-dark-font-style, inherit);
  font-weight: var(--shiki-dark-font-weight, inherit);
}
:root[data-theme="light"] .shiki,
:root[data-theme="light"] .shiki span {
  color: var(--shiki-light);
  font-style: var(--shiki-light-font-style, inherit);
  font-weight: var(--shiki-light-font-weight, inherit);
}

.how-code {
  background: transparent;
  margin: 24px 0;
  font-size: 14.5px;
  line-height: 25px;
}
.how-code pre.shiki {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 0 0 2.4rem;
  background: transparent !important;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  white-space: pre-wrap;
  word-break: break-word;
  position: relative;
}

.shiki-scroll { padding: 56px; background: var(--bg-2); }
.shiki-scroll pre.shiki {
  margin: 0;
  padding: 0 0 0 4.6rem;
  max-width: calc(80ch + 4.6rem);
  min-height: 100%;
  background: transparent !important;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 15px;
  line-height: 1.65;
  white-space: pre-wrap;
  word-break: break-word;
  position: relative;
}

.shiki code { counter-reset: step; counter-increment: step 0; }
.shiki .line::before {
  content: counter(step);
  counter-increment: step;
  display: inline-block;
  width: 2ch;
  margin-right: 1.6em;
  text-align: right;
  color: var(--fg-4);
  user-select: none;
}
.shiki-scroll .line { scroll-margin-top: 84px; }
.shiki-scroll .line::before {
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  width: 2.6rem;
  margin: 0;
  text-align: left;
}
.how-code .line::before {
  position: absolute;
  left: 0;
  width: 1.6rem;
  margin: 0;
  text-align: left;
  font-size: 12.5px;
}

.how-play {
  height: clamp(440px, 72vh, 720px);
  display: flex;
  padding: 40px;
}
.gomoku {
  flex: 1;
  min-height: 0;
  display: flex;
  flex-direction: column;
  align-items: center;
  gap: 10px;
}
.gomoku-grid {
  flex: 1;
  min-height: 0;
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  max-width: 100%;
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: repeat(15, 1fr);
  grid-template-rows: repeat(15, 1fr);
  gap: 1px;
  background: var(--rule-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 4px;
  container-type: inline-size;
}
.gomoku-cell:first-child { border-top-left-radius: 3px; }
.gomoku-cell:nth-child(15) { border-top-right-radius: 3px; }
.gomoku-cell:nth-child(211) { border-bottom-left-radius: 3px; }
.gomoku-cell:last-child { border-bottom-right-radius: 3px; }
.gomoku-cell {
  appearance: none;
  border: none;
  background: var(--bg-2);
  padding: 0;
  cursor: pointer;
  position: relative;
  overflow: visible;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  transition: background .08s ease;
}
.gomoku-cell:hover { background: var(--bg-3); }
.gomoku-cell.black,
.gomoku-cell.white { cursor: default; }
.gomoku-cell.black::after,
.gomoku-cell.white::after {
  content: '';
  width: 78%;
  aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
  border-radius: 50%;
}
.gomoku-cell.black::after {
  --glow: var(--acc-violet);
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 36% 30%, var(--acc-violet), color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-violet) 52%, black) 88%);
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5);
}
.gomoku-cell.white::after {
  --glow: var(--acc-mint);
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 36% 30%, var(--acc-mint), color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-mint) 52%, black) 88%);
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.45);
}
:root[data-theme="light"] .gomoku-cell.black::after {
  --glow: #3C3836;
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 36% 30%, #6A6560, #1B1A18 88%);
  box-shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
}
:root[data-theme="light"] .gomoku-cell.white::after {
  --glow: #BDAE93;
  background: radial-gradient(circle at 36% 30%, #FFFFFF, #ECE6D6 88%);
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(60, 56, 54, 0.18), 0 1px 2px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.22);
}
.gomoku-cell.win {
  z-index: 2;
}
.gomoku-cell.win::after {
  animation: gomoku-pulse 0.9s ease-in-out infinite;
}
.gomoku-cell.last {
  z-index: 1;
}
.gomoku-cell.last::after {
  box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--acc-amber), 0 0 9px 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-amber) 55%, transparent);
}
.gomoku-cell.mine::after {
  content: '💣';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 5.5cqw;
  line-height: 1;
  opacity: 0.82;
  animation: gomoku-reveal 0.45s ease-out both;
}
@keyframes gomoku-reveal {
  0% { transform: scale(0.4); opacity: 0; }
  100% { transform: scale(1); opacity: 0.82; }
}
.gomoku-cell.broken {
  cursor: not-allowed;
  z-index: 3;
}
.gomoku-cell.broken::after {
  content: '💥';
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 7.5cqw;
  line-height: 1;
  animation: gomoku-boom 1.4s ease-out;
}
@keyframes gomoku-pulse {
  0%, 100% { transform: scale(1); box-shadow: 0 0 0 0 transparent; }
  50% { transform: scale(1.16); box-shadow: 0 0 11px 2px var(--glow); }
}
@keyframes gomoku-boom {
  0% { content: '💣'; transform: scale(0.5); opacity: 0; }
  18% { content: '💣'; transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
  60% { content: '💣'; transform: scale(1); opacity: 1; }
  70% { content: '💥'; transform: scale(1.6); }
  100% { content: '💥'; transform: scale(1); }
}
.gomoku.thinking .gomoku-grid { pointer-events: none; }

## The command palette

Beneath the steps sits a command palette that searches the book — type and the list filters, the arrows move the focus, and each result names its kind. The focused row wears the mint tint.

=>

.cmd-wrap {
  margin-top: 56px;
  background: var(--bg-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 8px;
  overflow: hidden;
  max-width: 720px;
  margin-left: auto;
  margin-right: auto;
  box-shadow: 0 30px 80px -30px var(--shadow);
}
.cmd-input-wrap {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px;
  padding: 14px 18px;
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  font-family: var(--mono);
}
.cmd-input-wrap .prompt { color: var(--acc-mint); }
.cmd-input {
  flex: 1; background: transparent; border: none; outline: none;
  color: var(--fg); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 14px;
}
.cmd-input::placeholder { color: var(--fg-4); }
.cmd-list {
  max-height: 260px; overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 6px 0;
}
.cmd-item {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 22px 1fr auto;
  gap: 12px;
  align-items: center;
  padding: 9px 18px;
  cursor: pointer;
  color: var(--fg-2);
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px;
  transition: background .1s ease;
}
.cmd-item:hover, .cmd-item.focused {
  background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--acc-mint) 14%, transparent);
  color: var(--fg);
}
.cmd-glyph { color: var(--fg-4); }
.cmd-item.focused .cmd-glyph { color: var(--acc-mint); }
.cmd-kind {
  color: var(--fg-4); font-size: 11px;
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px;
}
.cmd-hi { color: var(--acc-mint); }
.cmd-foot {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
  padding: 8px 18px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  color: var(--fg-4);
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 11px;
}
.cmd-foot kbd {
  font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px;
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  padding: 1px 5px; border-radius: 3px;
  background: var(--bg-3);
  color: var(--fg-3);
}

## The install rows

Under the headline sits the install: one row per runtime. The rows are a plain stack in the mono face — no frame around them, no dividers between them. Each row is a button, sized to its content: it leads with the runtime's logo, gives the install command room to run, and ends with a copy icon that stays hidden until the row is hovered. The pressed row turns that copy icon into a mint check.

=>

.install-rows {
  margin-top: 40px;
  max-width: 560px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
}
.install-row {
  display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px;
  width: fit-content;
  max-width: 100%;
  padding: 7px 10px;
  margin-left: -10px;
  appearance: none;
  border: none;
  border-radius: 6px;
  background: none;
  color: inherit;
  font: inherit;
  text-align: left;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background .12s ease;
}
.install-row:hover { background: var(--bg-3); }
.rt-copy {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  opacity: 0;
  transition: opacity .12s ease, color .12s ease;
}
.install-row:hover .rt-copy { opacity: 1; }
.rt-copy.copied { opacity: 1; color: var(--acc-mint); }
.rt-mark {
  flex-shrink: 0;
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  width: 18px; height: 18px;
}
.rt-logo { display: inline-flex; }
.rt-mark svg { display: block; width: 18px; height: 18px; }
.rt-cmd {
  color: var(--fg); font-size: 13px;
  white-space: nowrap;
}

## The footer

The footer is a grid of link columns under the brand and its tagline.

=>

footer.foot {
  padding: 64px 0 40px;
  border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
}
.foot-grid {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-columns: 2fr 1fr 1fr 1fr;
  gap: 40px;
  margin-bottom: 40px;
}
@media (max-width: 880px) { .foot-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
.foot-col h4 {
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 11px;
  color: var(--fg-3);
  letter-spacing: 0.12em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  margin: 0 0 14px;
  font-weight: 500;
}
.foot-col ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
.foot-col li { margin-bottom: 8px; font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; }
.foot-col a { color: var(--fg-2); transition: color .15s ease; }
.foot-col a:hover { color: var(--acc-mint); }
.foot-mark .tag {
  font-family: var(--display);
  font-style: italic;
  font-weight: 300;
  font-size: 18px;
  color: var(--fg-2);
  line-height: 1.5;
  max-width: 40ch;
  margin-top: 16px;
}
.brand {
  display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 7px;
  font-family: var(--mono);
  font-size: 19px; font-weight: 500;
  color: var(--fg);
}
.brand .b-mark {
  display: inline-flex;
  color: var(--acc-mint);
}
.brand .b-mark svg { width: 20px; height: 20px; }

## The tweaks panel

The tweaks panel is the small control that tries the light theme's accent families and the hero title's colour count. It sits fixed in the lower-right corner, above the page, dressed in the same tokens as the chrome so it reads at home in either theme. Its options fall into two groups under their own headings — the accent families, then the title. Each row names an option beside a strip of its colours, and the one in play wears a raised, bordered look. A swatch carries a faint inner ring, so a pale colour still shows its edge. The panel scrolls within its own height when the options outrun the screen.

=>

.tweaks {
  position: fixed;
  right: 18px; bottom: 18px;
  z-index: 200;
  width: 208px;
  max-height: calc(100vh - 36px);
  overflow-y: auto;
  padding: 10px;
  background: var(--bg-2);
  border: 1px solid var(--rule-2);
  border-radius: 10px;
  box-shadow: 0 20px 50px -20px var(--shadow);
  font-family: var(--mono);
}
.tweaks-head {
  margin: 2px 4px 8px;
  font-size: 10px;
  letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  text-transform: uppercase;
  color: var(--fg-4);
}
.tweaks-opts + .tweaks-head { margin-top: 14px; }
.tweaks-opts { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; }
.tweaks-opt {
  display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px;
  padding: 7px 8px;
  border: 1px solid transparent;
  border-radius: 7px;
  background: none;
  color: var(--fg-2);
  font: inherit; font-size: 12px;
  text-align: left;
  cursor: pointer;
  transition: background .12s ease, border-color .12s ease, color .12s ease;
}
.tweaks-opt:hover { background: var(--bg-3); color: var(--fg); }
.tweaks-opt.active {
  background: var(--bg-3);
  border-color: var(--rule-2);
  color: var(--fg);
}
.tweaks-sw { display: inline-flex; gap: 3px; }
.tweaks-dot {
  width: 11px; height: 11px;
  border-radius: 50%;
  box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 1px #0000001A;
}

